      "id": "rnn2qdf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Levels of Organization in the Human Body"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Structural hierarchy in humans follows: Cells → Tissues → Organs → Organ Systems → Organism.",
        "The Circulatory System uses blood to transport oxygen, nutrients, and metabolic waste products across the body.",
        "The Nervous System offers rapid electrical signaling, while the Endocrine System regulates long-term body functions chemically via hormones.",
        "The Excretory System removes nitrogenous metabolic waste through nephrons in the kidneys.",
        "The Digestive System processes nutrients through mechanical breakdown and enzymatic hydrolysis."
      ],
      "id": "4gi0dfa"
    },
