    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequently tested units: Neuron is the basic unit of the nervous system; Nephron is the structural and functional unit of the kidney.",
        "Pulmonary Artery carries deoxygenated blood to lungs, while Pulmonary Vein carries oxygenated blood to the heart (exceptions to general artery/vein rules).",
        "Endocrine glands are ductless and release hormones directly into the bloodstream, whereas Exocrine glands use ducts.",
        "Digestive enzymes: Pepsin acts in an acidic pH in the stomach, while Trypsin acts in an alkaline pH in the small intestine."
      ],
      "id": "e9eikbx"
